ralia (Orica)","lat":-23.8,"lon":151.2,"cap":"30kt"},{"name":"Newcastle, Australia (Orica)","lat":-32.9,"lon":151.8,"cap":"12kt"},{"name":"Burrup Peninsula, Australia (Burrup Fert.)","lat":-20.6,"lon":116.7,"cap":"80kt"}],"phos":[{"name":"OCP Morocco (Jorf Lasfar)","lat":33.1,"lon":-8.6},{"name":"OCP Morocco (Safi)","lat":32.3,"lon":-9.2},{"name":"GCT Tunisia (Gabes)","lat":33.9,"lon":9.6},{"name":"JPMC Jordan (Aqaba)","lat":29.5,"lon":35},{"name":"Maaden Saudi Arabia","lat":27,"lon":49.6},{"name":"PhosAgro Russia","lat":67.9,"lon":33.1},{"name":"Mosaic USA (Florida)","lat":27.9,"lon":-82.3},{"name":"OCP Senegal (Taiba)","lat":14.9,"lon":-16.9},{"name":"China (Yunnan/Guizhou)","lat":26,"lon":106.7},{"name":"Israel Chemicals (Rotem)","lat":30.8,"lon":35.2},{"name":"PT Petrokimia Indonesia","lat":-7.2,"lon":112.6}],"mop":[{"name":"Saskatchewan, Canada (Nutrien/Mosaic)","lat":52,"lon":-105.5},{"name":"Belaruskali, Belarus","lat":53,"lon":28.5},{"name":"Uralkali, Russia (Berezniki)","lat":59.4,"lon":56.8},{"name":"Dead Sea Works, Israel","lat":31.2,"lon":35.4},{"name":"Arab Potash, Jordan","lat":31.2,"lon":35.6},{"name":"Qinghai Salt Lake, China","lat":36.9,"lon":100.1},{"name":"Yunnan, China","lat":25.1,"lon":101.5},{"name":"Laos (K-MICON)","lat":17.5,"lon":104.5},{"name":"Germany (K+S)","lat":51.5,"lon":10},{"name":"Bolivia (developing)","lat":-19.5,"lon":-65.7},{"name":"Sergipe, Brazil (Vale)","lat":-10.7,"lon":-37.4}],"facts":[{"n":"Belarus","f":"Belaruskali is one of the world's largest potash producers. Production sanctioned since 2021 following geopolitical events.","t":["Major MOP exporter","Belaruskali","Sanctions-impacted"]},{"n":"Canada","f":"World's largest potash exporter (~35Mt capacity). Nutrien and Mosaic dominate the Saskatchewan basin.","t":["#1 MOP exporter","Saskatchewan mines","Nutrien/Mosaic"]},{"n":"China","f":"The world's largest fertilizer producer and consumer. Export quotas on urea and phosphates are watched globally as a key price signal.","t":["Major urea exporter","Quota-controlled","Largest fertilizer market"]},{"n":"Germany","f":"Major European hub. Historically large domestic production but high TTF gas costs have made local output uncompetitive vs imports.","t":["European hub","High TTF gas cost","Net importer"]},{"n":"India","f":"World's 2nd largest fertilizer market. Imports ~8Mt urea, ~8Mt DAP, ~4Mt MOP annually. Sets the price floor for many global markets.","t":["Major importer","Urea/DAP/MOP buyer","Sets price floors"]},{"n":"Indonesia","f":"PT Pupuk Kaltim at Bontang is the primary production hub. Major urea producer for domestic use and growing export volumes.","t":["Pupuk Kaltim","Bontang NH3 48kt","Growing exporter"]},{"n":"Iran","f":"Major urea producer with some of the world's cheapest gas. Exports flow despite sanctions via indirect routes. Bandar Imam Khomeini is the key terminal.","t":["Cheap gas feedstock","Sanctioned flows","Bandar I. Khomeini"]},{"n":"Jordan","f":"JPMC operates Aqaba with 40kt NH3 storage. Arab Potash mines Dead Sea potash. Important phosphate rock and acid exporter.","t":["Phosphoric acid/DAP","NH3 terminal 40kt","Dead Sea potash"]},{"n":"South Korea","f":"Major NH3 import hub. Lotte Fine Chemicals at Ulsan (60kt). Yeosu (Namhae, 50kt). Key downstream industrial consumer.","t":["NH3 terminal 60kt","Major importer","Lotte/Namhae"]},{"n":"Malaysia","f":"PETRONAS-backed Fertilizer Malaysia Berhad (SAMUR) at Kerteh. Gas-advantaged production. Exports urea and ammonia regionally.","t":["Petronas gas advantage","Kerteh 29kt NH3","Regional exporter"]},{"n":"Morocco","f":"OCP controls ~30% of world phosphate reserves. Jorf Lasfar is the world's largest fertilizer complex. #1 phosphoric acid, DAP and MAP exporter.","t":["#1 phosphate exporter","OCP state producer","Jorf Lasfar complex"]},{"n":"Oman","f":"OMIFCO at Sur — joint venture producing urea and ammonia. 60kt NH3 terminal. Major supplier to India and East Africa.","t":["OMIFCO Sur plant","60kt NH3 terminal","India/Africa supplier"]},{"n":"Nigeria","f":"Indorama and Notore produce urea using domestic gas. Significant potential but output hampered by gas supply reliability issues.","t":["Indorama/Notore","Gas reliability risk","West Africa hub"]},{"n":"Norway","f":"Headquarters of Yara International — the world's largest fertilizer company by sales. Multiple NH3 terminals globally.","t":["Yara HQ","Global trader","Multiple NH3 terminals"]},{"n":"Qatar","f":"QAFCO at Mesaieed — one of the world's largest single urea complexes. North Field gas is among the cheapest globally. ~5Mt/yr N exports.","t":["Ultra-low gas cost","QAFCO 165kt NH3","5Mt+ N exports"]},{"n":"Russia","f":"World's largest urea exporter (~7Mt/yr). Ultra-cheap domestic gas gives a massive cost advantage. Key terminals at Taman and Sillamäe. Also a leading MAP exporter.","t":["#1 urea exporter","MAP exporter","Gas ~USD 2-4/MMBtu"]},{"n":"Saudi Arabia","f":"Ma'aden and SABIC operate large complexes at Al-Jubail and Ras Al-Khair. Exports DAP, MAP, urea and ammonia with heavily subsidised gas feedstock.","t":["DAP/MAP/urea exporter","Subsidised gas","Al-Jubail complex"]},{"n":"Trinidad & Tobago","f":"Point Lisas hub — CF Industries (80kt NH3) and Nutrien (100kt NH3). Key Atlantic supplier to USA and Latin America.","t":["CF Industries/Nutrien","Atlantic NH3 hub","Point Lisas"]},{"n":"UAE","f":"FERTIL at Ruwais (40kt NH3) and ADNOC Fertilizers operations. A key hub for Middle East fertilizer trading and logistics.","t":["NH3 terminal 40kt","FERTIL/ADNOC","Trading hub"]},{"n":"Tunisia","f":"GCT produces phosphoric acid, DAP and TSP at Gabes from domestic phosphate rock from Gafsa. Key supplier to Europe.","t":["Phosphoric acid","DAP/TSP exporter","GCT producer"]},{"n":"Egypt","f":"Egypt FOB is the global urea benchmark price for the Atlantic basin. EBIC ammonia terminal at Ain Sokhna (35kt). Major N exporter.","t":["Urea price benchmark","EBIC 35kt NH3","Atlantic basin supplier"]},{"n":"Brazil","f":"World's largest fertilizer importer, taking ~40Mt/year across urea, MAP, DAP and MOP. Critical demand signal for global markets.","t":["Largest importer","All products","Key demand signal"]},{"n":"Algeria","f":"Emerging urea exporter using domestic Saharan gas. Fertial plants at Annaba and Arzew. Growing exports to Mediterranean.","t":["Emerging urea exporter","Fertial producer","Low-cost gas"]},{"n":"Australia","f":"Net fertilizer importer. Key NH3 receiving terminals at Burrup Peninsula (Yara, 80kt) and Kwinana (CSBP, 40kt).","t":["NH3 terminal 80kt","Net importer","Yara/CSBP terminals"]},{"n":"Argentina","f":"Profertil at Bahia Blanca (20kt NH3) produces urea using Patagonian gas for domestic and regional export.","t":["Profertil Bahia Blanca","NH3 terminal 20kt","Regional supplier"]},{"n":"Bangladesh","f":"KAFCO at Chittagong — 20kt NH3 terminal. Produces urea from domestic gas for local agricultural use.","t":["KAFCO Chittagong","NH3 terminal 20kt","Domestic producer"]}]}